<title>GERMANY: Bonn to check welfare recipients' savings - Bild.</title>
<headline>Bonn to check welfare recipients' savings - Bild.</headline>
<dateline>BONN 1997-04-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Germany's Health Ministry plans to begin checking more closely on welfare recipients' bank accounts and other assets, the Bild newspaper said on Friday.</p>
<p>Health Minister Horst Seehofer plans to order authorities to use the Finance Ministry to check the interest earned on recipients' bank accounts, the mass circulation daily said.</p>
<p>Social payments would be cut off for recipients who hide assets, the report said. German law says welfare recipients may have no more than 2,500 marks in savings.</p>
<p>-- Bonn Newsroom, +49-228 260 97 150</p>
